he suited tiles. For example, if I have two of the same tile. But I have only one of each. So maybe the pair is formed by drawing a tile. For example, if I discard a tile, and then draw a duplicate.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the hand is aiming for a Seven Pairs pattern. But Seven Pairs requires seven pairs. Currently, I have no pairs. So that's unlikely.\n\nAnother possibility is to form a hand with multiple pungs. For example, if I can get pungs of F3, F4, J1, J2, but I have only one of each. So that's not possible.\n\nLooking at the unshown tiles, maybe there are opportunities. For example, F4 is the prevailing wind (West Wind). If I can get another F4, that would form a pung, giving a Prevalent Wind fan (2 points). Since I have one F4, keeping it might help. Similarly, my seat wind is South (F2), but I have F3 and F4. So maybe not relevant here.\n\nAnother angle: the current hand has a mix of suits and honors. It's possible that the player is aiming for a Half Flush (all in one suit plus honors), but with the current hand, it's mixed. Alternatively, All Types (all suits and honors), which is 6 points. But that's not enough for the minimum 8 points. Wait, the minimum is 8 points. So the player needs to reach at least 8 points. Let me check the possible patterns.\n\nThe kong of W8 is worth 4 points (Concealed Kong). If the rest of the hand can contribute another 4 points, that would make 8. For example, if the remaining hand has a Fully Concealed Hand (4 points), but that's not possible if there are any exposed melds. Wait, the kong is a concealed meld, so it's part of the concealed hand. If all other melds are concealed, then Fully Concealed Hand gives 4 points. Let's see: the remaining hand needs to form four melds and a pair, all concealed. Let's see if that's possible.\n\nCurrent hand: W1, W4, T4, T7, B3, B4, B6, F3, F4, J1, J2. Need to form four melds and a pair. Let's see:\n\nPossible melds:\n\n- W1, W4: Maybe a chow? No, they are not consecutive. Or a pair? No